From: nura-builds
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/mdp5: black interface underflow colour

mdp5 sets the interface's underflow colour to 0xff, blue: what the panel shows for pixels the
MDP couldn't fetch in time. On MSM8226 every enable has a few frames of underruns (the
interface starts before the planes are committed, about ten underrun interrupts), which showed
as blue flashes before the boot splash and at each screen-on. Black instead.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_encoder.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_encoder.c
index eaba3b2d73b5..cb66037ef783 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_encoder.c
@@ -101,7 +101,8 @@ static void mdp5_vid_encoder_mode_set(struct drm_encoder *encoder,
 	mdp5_write(mdp5_kms, REG_MDP5_INTF_DISPLAY_VSTART_F0(intf), display_v_start);
 	mdp5_write(mdp5_kms, REG_MDP5_INTF_DISPLAY_VEND_F0(intf), display_v_end);
 	mdp5_write(mdp5_kms, REG_MDP5_INTF_BORDER_COLOR(intf), 0);
-	mdp5_write(mdp5_kms, REG_MDP5_INTF_UNDERFLOW_COLOR(intf), 0xff);
+	/* black, not blue: underruns at each enable showed as blue flashes (MSM8226) */
+	mdp5_write(mdp5_kms, REG_MDP5_INTF_UNDERFLOW_COLOR(intf), 0);
 	mdp5_write(mdp5_kms, REG_MDP5_INTF_HSYNC_SKEW(intf), dtv_hsync_skew);
 	mdp5_write(mdp5_kms, REG_MDP5_INTF_POLARITY_CTL(intf), ctrl_pol);
 	mdp5_write(mdp5_kms, REG_MDP5_INTF_ACTIVE_HCTL(intf),
